From 501a6bb947f8720d3d503c3355cacce080b82b22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Lesperance <lespea@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:56:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Don't switch %fs to pthread_teb for system threads on
 x86_64.

System threads created by PsCreateSystemThread() never run
signal_init_thread()/call_init_thunk(), so amd64_thread_data->pthread_teb
is never initialized and stays NULL. In WoW64 processes (fs32_sel != 0)
init_handler() then loads %fs with 0, and the first libc TLS access in the
handler (NtCurrentTeb() -> pthread_getspecific()) faults at %fs:0x10.

This makes every 32-bit process with winewayland's event dispatcher
system thread crash with SIGSEGV on exit, when wineserver sends SIGQUIT
and quit_handler() runs on that thread. SIGUSR1 (usr1_handler) is
affected the same way.

System threads never leave the Unix side, so %fs still holds the libc
TLS base and there is nothing to restore. Upstream avoids this because
init_handler() returns early for threads without amd64 thread data; this
is the equivalent for the 11.0 backport, matching what 0031 does for gs
on i386.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index cd6ba849cc6..8482cfe470f 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -928,7 +928,10 @@ static inline ucontext_t *init_handler( void *sigcontext )
     {
         struct amd64_thread_data *thread_data = (struct amd64_thread_data *)&get_current_teb()->GdiTebBatch;
         thread_data->syscall_dispatch = 0; /* SYSCALL_DISPATCH_FILTER_ALLOW */
-        if (fs32_sel) arch_prctl( ARCH_SET_FS, thread_data->pthread_teb );
+        /* system threads never run PE code, so %fs still holds the libc TLS base
+         * and pthread_teb is never initialized for them */
+        if (fs32_sel && !((struct ntdll_thread_data *)thread_data)->system_thread)
+            arch_prctl( ARCH_SET_FS, thread_data->pthread_teb );
     }
 #elif defined __APPLE__
     {
-- 
2.56.0

